      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014. Published by Elsevier Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Headache is a clinical diagnosis linked to a number of medical and surgical disorders. A common etiology has not yet been established. It would seem that these cases can be related to some degree of cerebral venous outflow obstruction. We report 2 cases of chronic superior sagittal sinus thrombosis causing isolated intracranial hypertension. The patients were treated with intrasinus thrombolytic therapy."
      },
